/*
A CNAME chain that ends in a denial at another zone (issue #186).

The CNAME is signed by `cdsrc.`, and what says its target has nothing is the
denial in the authority section, signed by the target's zone. RFC 6840 section
5.8 has the AD bit cover the relevant negative records as well as the answer,
so the denial is checked at the zone holding the end of the chain - the name
the rcode is about (RFC 6604 section 3) - the way a bare NODATA or NXDOMAIN is.

Generated - `testdata/gen/sign_fixtures.py`, scenario `cname_denial`.
*/

